# Testing

- One xUnit test project per `src/` project it covers:
  `PickMeWhatToListen.Domain.Tests`, `PickMeWhatToListen.Application.Tests`,
  plus `PickMeWhatToListen.ArchitectureTests` for cross-cutting layer rules
  (NetArchTest).
- `Application` tests must not touch a real database — use the
  `FakeArtistRepository` / `FixedRandomProvider` test doubles under
  `tests/PickMeWhatToListen.Application.Tests/TestDoubles/` (or add new ones
  following the same pattern) instead of EF Core / SQLite.
- `ArchitectureTests` is not optional scaffolding — it's the mechanical
  enforcement of `ARCHITECTURE.md`. Any change to layer boundaries must come
  with an updated or new rule there, in the same change.
- Prefer `[Theory]`/`[InlineData]` over copy-pasted `[Fact]`s for the same
  behavior with different inputs (see `ArtistTests.Create_ThrowsOnEmptyName`).
- Run `dotnet test` before considering any change done. CI
  (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) runs the full suite plus
  `dotnet format --verify-no-changes` on `windows-latest`.
